      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T10:29:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sharing checks with Soong\u0027s `GenerateAndroidBuildActions` is not correct. Some of these call `a.WalkPayloadDeps` on the Soong module graph, which is distinct from the Bazel graph. Others validate Android.bp properties, but they should be done by the Bazel apex rule implementation on the BUILD attributes instead.\n\nWhen Bazel takes over this `apexBundle` in mixed builds, all of the information needed to fulfil `apexBundle` should come from the Bazel query responses, which has information about the Bazel transitive dependencies of this APEX\u0027s payload. `ProcessBazelQueryResponse` should be practically mapping query responses to `apexBundle` fields directly. If Bazel doesn\u0027t export the information, then we\u0027ll need to implement them in the Starlark rule and return them in `ApexInfo` (or another provider).\n\nConcretely speaking:\n\n- `checkApexAvailability`: this calls WalkPayloadDeps, and should be handled on the Bazel side, and not called in ProcessBazelQueryResponse. b/218841706\n- `checkUpdatable`: the property checks (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/apex/apex.go;l\u003d2672-2684;drc\u003da477a7a86a3198ab873a57bb95411b5a3574ba91) should be done in the bazel apex rule. `checkJavaStableSdkVersion` and `checkClasspathFragments` walk the Soong deps, so they shouldn\u0027t be here.\n- `checkMinSdkVersion`, `checkStaticLinkingToStubLibraries`, `checkStaticExecutables`: similar to `checkApexAvailability`.\n- tests property check: similar to `checkUpdatable` property checks and should be done in Bazel Starlark.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1806,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1808,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "f3d1302203f4be52941370df6a82f778f84b530c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
